id: pm-y4v90c
title: Preserve surrogate pairs in bounded extension error diagnostics
description: "describeHandlerError and readHandlerStringField in src/core/extensions/extension-hook-runtime.ts currently bound normalized message/code/remediation with UTF-16 slice. A valid emoji starting at the cutoff becomes a lone high surrogate (298 ASCII characters plus an emoji for the 299-unit message prefix, or 299 ASCII characters plus an emoji for 300-unit metadata). Reuse the shared Unicode-safe prefix primitive without changing field length budgets or mutating the original error. This is a separate diagnostic truncation boundary from pm-gh1624 raw output admission."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T19:42:21.007Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T21:06:42.169Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T21:06:41.469Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T21:06:41.469Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Prove valid astral characters survive cutoff boundaries through the public extension test harness; Preserve 300-unit diagnostic bounds and the original error; Retain no-handler and typed refusal contracts
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: describeHandlerError and readHandlerStringField cut with unicodeSafePrefix at the unchanged 300-unit budgets; public-harness regression with a fitting-pair control and a proven negative control.
expected_result: Astral characters at the 299/300-unit cutoff never become lone surrogates and the thrown error is untouched.
actual_result: "298-char message plus emoji yields 298 chars and an ellipsis, 299-char code/remediation plus emoji yield 299 chars, all fields well-formed; the spec fails with the fix stashed."
