comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T19:42:21.007Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: live all-state corpus3155 records plus request-specific searches for extension diagnostic Unicode truncation and surrogate truncation, current open/in_progress inventories, and full pm-gh1478 data/comments/history. Closed pm-gh1478 implements bounded output prefixes; active pm-gh1624 owns raw output admission. Neither owns these two extension-hook diagnostic slices. Static boundary reproduction produces a lone surrogate from valid emoji text; no source change or claim is included in this follow-up."
  "2026-11-01T20:09:26.184Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation: describeHandlerError and readHandlerStringField (src/core/extensions/extension-hook-runtime.ts) now cut with the shared unicodeSafePrefix primitive. The 300-unit budgets are unchanged (message: 299 units plus the ellipsis; code/remediation: 300 units), and the thrown error object is never rewritten.\n\nRegression (tests/unit/extensions/extensions-runtime.spec.ts, through createExtensionTestHarness): 298 ASCII + emoji message now yields 298 chars + ellipsis (was a lone high surrogate); 299 ASCII + emoji code/remediation yield 299 chars; every field isWellFormed(); a pair that fits inside the bound survives intact. Negative control: with the source change stashed the new test fails (1 failed), restored it passes.\n"
